## What We Learned

- JPA provides the standard persistence API.
- Hibernate is one of the implementations of JPA.
- Spring Data JPA makes database operations much simpler.
- Repository interfaces reduce the amount of code we need to write.
- Hibernate automatically generates SQL based on JPA annotations.

---

## Conclusion

This hands-on demonstrates how JPA, Hibernate, and Spring Data JPA work together in a Spring Boot application. JPA provides the standard, Hibernate implements it, and Spring Data JPA simplifies database operations by reducing boilerplate code. Using these technologies together makes application development faster, cleaner, and easier to maintain.
